# VFS_LEAF_CATEGORIES_VERIFICATION_SPRINT.todo
# Professional Sprint — Verify All 20 Leaf Categories Return Correct Products
# Reference: VFS Architecture, MASTER_TASKLIST Critical Path, catalogue-index.json
# Created: 2026-03-27

---

## 🎯 Sprint Objective

**Verify that all 20 leaf categories correctly retrieve and display expected products using the VFS-based catalogue system, with a systematic, automated pathway to ensure continued correctness.**

**Current State:** VFS infrastructure exists and appears complete (catalogue-index.json has all 20 leaf categories mapped). Products page uses VFS for queries. However, there is no systematic verification that each category returns the expected products.

**Target State:** 
- All 20 leaf categories tested and verified to return correct products
- Automated test suite that validates VFS data integrity
- Systematic pathway (CI/CD integration) to catch regressions
- Documentation of expected product counts per category
- Validation script that can be run on-demand or scheduled

---

## 🧪 TEST-FIRST MANDATE

This sprint **MUST begin with tests** that define the expected behavior (which products belong to which categories) and **MUST end with tests** that verify the implementation. Test execution results determine sprint completion status.

---

## 📋 Scope Contracts

---

### Scope Contract 1: VFS Data Integrity Baseline
**Rationale:** Before verifying products, we must confirm the VFS data structure is complete and consistent. This is the foundation for all category verification.

**Scope:**
- [ ] Run build-catalogue-index.mjs and confirm successful completion
- [ ] Validate all 20 leaf slugs exist in slugToIdMap
- [ ] Validate all 26 nodes (headers + leaves) exist in slotMetadataMap
- [ ] Verify no orphaned children (all children IDs exist in slotMetadataMap)
- [ ] Document the complete catalogue structure for reference

**Files at Risk:**
- `data/catalogue-index.json` - VFS data manifest
- `data/catalogue.ts` - VFS utility functions
- `scripts/build-catalogue-index.mjs` - Build script

**Regression Tests Required:**
- [ ] VFS build script completes without validation errors
  - **Verification:** `node scripts/build-catalogue-index.mjs`
  - **Expected:** "✅ VALIDATION PASSED" message
- [ ] All 20 leaf categories have ID mappings
  - **Verification:** `npm test -- tests/vfs/leaf-categories-exist.test.ts`
- [ ] All slotMetadataMap entries have valid children arrays
  - **Verification:** `npm test -- tests/vfs/metadata-integrity.test.ts`

**Out of Scope:**
- Modifying the build script logic (it already has validation)
- Changing the VFS structure or hierarchy
- Modifying any product schemas

---

### Scope Contract 2: Leaf Category Product Count Baseline
**Rationale:** We need to know the expected product count for each of the 20 leaf categories to verify correctness. This creates a referenceable baseline.

**Scope:**
- [ ] Query Sanity for actual product counts per leaf category
- [ ] Document expected product count for each of the 20 leaf categories
- [ ] Verify products have correct `catalogueLocationKeys` in Sanity
- [ ] Identify any products with missing or incorrect category assignments
- [ ] Create a baseline manifest file with expected counts

**Files at Risk:**
- `sanity/lib/products/getProductsByVfsKeys.ts` - Product fetching
- `sanity/lib/products/getSelectedProducts.ts` - Filtered product fetching
- `data/catalogue-index.json` - Reference for category IDs

**Regression Tests Required:**
- [ ] Sanity connection and query execution works
  - **Verification:** `npm test -- tests/integration/sanity-connection.test.ts`
- [ ] All leaf category IDs return products (or confirm intentionally empty)
  - **Verification:** `npm test -- tests/integration/leaf-category-products.test.ts`
- [ ] Product catalogueLocationKeys match VFS structure
  - **Verification:** `npm test -- tests/integration/product-keys-validation.test.ts`

**Out of Scope:**
- Fixing data issues in Sanity (document only, fix in separate sprint)
- Modifying product schemas
- Changing GROQ query logic

**Architecture Decision:**
- Document-only for data issues; do not modify production data in this sprint
- Create follow-up sprint for data cleanup if issues found

---

### Scope Contract 3: Automated Category Verification Test Suite
**Rationale:** Create a systematic, automated pathway to verify all 20 categories. This is the core deliverable that ensures continued correctness.

**Scope:**
- [ ] Create test file for all 20 leaf categories
- [ ] Test each category returns expected products (based on baseline)
- [ ] Test VFS unrollDescendantKeys returns correct keys for each category
- [ ] Test slug-to-ID resolution for all 20 slugs
- [ ] Create aggregate test that validates entire catalogue integrity

**Files at Risk:**
- `tests/` directory structure - New test files will be added
- `data/catalogue.ts` - May need exports for testing
- `package.json` - May need test scripts

